@@ -129,3 +129,5 @@
 Truck properties, Addons and Frame addons each have a Show changed only toggle button. It includes preview/staged differences from current files and applied values differing from preserved originals. In Frame addons this includes fuel and tracked price/rank/exploration changes. It combines with header filters and stays enabled across reloads and addon-view switches; turning it off retains other filters. The toggle changes visibility only: Stage and global reset actions still include hidden rows.
 
 Frame addon fuel multiplication skips explicit zero capacities, rounds nonzero results to 5 L, and uses 0-10,000 L bounds. Restoring fuel keeps the exact original integer capacity without rounding it. Truck fuel bounds are unchanged. Truck properties reset also preserves original attribute absence: an introduced UnlockByExploration=false is staged as an attribute removal, so Start no longer retains Not present -> false after reset/apply. XML difference auditing compares parsed properties and ignores whitespace, line-ending and encoding-only differences; real added/removed/changed attributes remain listed.
+
+Editors > Various has an Ignore ice on all tires toggle. On previews IsIgnoreIce="true" on every TruckWheels/TruckTires/TruckTire/WheelFriction, adding local overrides for inherited tires, and on friction templates (including local tire templates) across base and DLC wheel files. Off previews restoration of preserved original ice settings, retaining chained tires. Stage changes persists the snapshot; Start > Apply pending changes writes only the updated overlay. Revert unstaged/staged controls follow the other editors. Shared presets include this preview and staging. Pack a new PAK and install manually.
